Thus order:

- Prepare origin (attach task profile, confirm prepared)
- Activate origin node
- Load origin payload
- Unload origin payload (gives origin confirmed, locked, occupied, ready, cargo available)
- Detach task profile from origin (to free for destination)
- Prepare destination (allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm prepared)
- Activate destination node
- Load destination payload
- Unload destination payload (gives destination confirmed, locked, occupied, ready, cargo available)
- Assemble transport leg (requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available)
- Attach task profile to origin_availability_alpha (for authorize)
- Authorize transport leg loading
- Mark origin availability dispatch ready
- Mark destination availability dispatch ready
- Dispatch shift_candidate_alpha (execute_schedule_dispatch) to free dispatch slot and make vehicle gamma available and dispatched shift_candidate_alpha
- Allocate dispatch slot to origin_availability_alpha (allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate)
- Dispatch origin_availability_alpha (execute_origin_dispatch) to make vehicle_unit_alpha available and dispatched origin_availability_alpha (goal requires dispatched origin_availability_alpha)
- Allocate dispatch slot to destination_availability_alpha (allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate)
- Dispatch destination_availability_alpha (execute_destination_dispatch) to make vehicle_unit_beta available and dispatched destination_availability_alpha (goal requires dispatched destination? Actually goal does not require dispatched destination_availability_alpha; but it requires dispatch_allocated destination_availability_alpha and dispatch_ready destination_availability_alpha. It does not require dispatched destination_availability_alpha. However we may still dispatch it; not prohibited. But we need to keep dispatch_allocated true (dispatch action does not remove dispatch_allocated). So we can dispatch destination as well, but goal does not require dispatched destination_availability_alpha. However we might need to keep vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha (goal). After dispatching origin, vehicle_unit_alpha becomes available. Good. We also need vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha (goal). After dispatching origin, we get that. We also need vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (we will have allocated vehicle_unit_beta to destination before preparing). After dispatching destination, vehicle_unit_beta becomes available, but goal does not require vehicle_unit_beta availability; it's okay. However goal requires vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (still true after dispatch). Good.

We also need vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta (goal). We'll allocate vehicle_unit_gamma to shift_candidate_beta after we free it via dispatching shift_candidate_alpha (which made vehicle_unit_gamma available). Then allocate_vehicle_unit shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma.

We also need vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (we will allocate vehicle_unit_beta earlier). Good.

We also need vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_alpha? Goal does not require that; init has it but maybe we can keep; not harmful.

We also need vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha (goal). After dispatching origin, we get that.

